---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy | Nether"
  description="What information Nether uses, how browser storage and contact options work, and how to ask a privacy question."
>
  <main class="archive-page plain-page">
    <header class="archive-header">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p>
        This policy describes the information handled by the current Nether
        website and what happens when you follow a link away from it.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Information this site uses</h2>
      <p>
        Nether does not ask you to create an account. This build does not
        include an analytics service or advertising tracker. The site code does
        not set cookies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Search uses a Pagefind index included with the site and runs in your
        browser. On the search page, a search can be included in the page URL
        as a <code>q</code> parameter. As with other page requests, that URL may
        be visible to the infrastructure serving the site; this project does
        not identify the live host's logging or retention practices.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        The theme control saves your light or dark preference in this
        browser's local storage under <code>nether-theme</code>. The site reads
        that value on later visits so it can restore your choice. It is not a
        cookie and stays in the browser until you clear it or your browser
        removes site data.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have not chosen a theme, the site uses your device's system
        preference. No account or profile is created from this setting.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Contact messages</h2>
      <p>
        If a contact form is enabled for the current build, it sends the name,
        email address, and message you enter to the HTTPS form endpoint
        configured for the site. The project does not name that provider or
        store form submissions in a site database. If a direct email link is
        shown, choosing it opens your email service and its handling applies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nether does not set a retention period for messages. The configured
        form or email service may keep information under its own terms and
        privacy policy. Check that service's policy for details.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        Product pages link to Shopee, Lazada, and Amazon. Those stores operate
        independently and may use their own cookies, analytics, or other
        technologies after you leave Nether. Their privacy notices and terms
        govern your activity there. Some product links may be affiliate links;
        see the <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> page for details.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        You can clear the saved theme preference using your browser's site-data
        controls. Depending on where you live and which laws apply, you may
        also have rights to ask for access to, correction of, or deletion of
        personal information, or to object to or limit certain uses. Those
        rights depend on the circumstances and on the service that received
        the information.
      </p>
      <p>
        To ask a privacy question or make a request, use the contact option
        available on the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page. I will handle
        requests as required by applicable data protection law. This statement
        does not claim that a particular law applies in every location.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="plain-page-section">
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If the site's data practices change, I will update this page and its
        date. The <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> and
        <a href="/disclosure/">Disclosure</a> pages explain related site
        practices.
      </p>
    </section>
    <p class="legal-updated">
      Last updated <time datetime="2026-11-02">November 2, 2026</time>.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
